d 'XTDOSEKC': module to estimate dynamic nonlinear panel EKC with difference-of-sigmoids and trends
d
d  xtdosekc implements Amoroso, Garcia-Martos and Koopman (2026,
d The Econometrics Journal, doi:10.1093/ectj/utag037). The
d Environmental Kuznets Curve is modelled as a difference of two
d logistic functions (economic-growth and green-transition effects)
d with country fixed effects and country stochastic trends.
d Parameters are estimated by penalised profile likelihood with an
d exact-diffuse Kalman filter and a Mata port of the L-BFGS-B
d optimiser, which reproduces the published estimates. Inference
d uses the Stoffer-Wall state-space bootstrap. The command also
d provides the static, linear-trend and single-equation variants,
d turning points, residual diagnostics, a dynamic factor model of
d the trends, penalty sensitivity and integration tests,
d journal-style tables with LaTeX export, and all of the paper's
d figures. 
d
d KW:  panel data
d KW: environmental Kuznets curve
d
d Requires: Stata version 15
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261123
d
d Author:   Merwan Roudane, NA
d Support: email  merwanroudane920@@gmail.com
d
